+/-- FV_7zip G1: a directory entry as `getdents64(2)` reports it (`struct linux_dirent64`, `include/linux/dirent.h`;
+`fs/readdir.c` `filldir64`): its inode number (`d_ino`), the position after it (`d_off`), its type (`d_type`, masked
+with `S_DT_MASK`, 4 bits) and its name, which the kernel requires to be 1 to `PATH_MAX - 1` bytes without a `/`
