+`XSAVE` reads `XSTATE_BV` and saves each component of `RFBM`, `MXCSR` and `MXCSR_MASK` with SSE or AVX, in the
+standard format (`xsaveRuns`), then writes `XSTATE_BV` as `(OLD_BV AND NOT RFBM) OR (XINUSE AND RFBM)`. `XSAVEC`
+saves the components of `TO_BE_SAVED`, `RFBM AND XINUSE` with SSE whenever `MXCSR` is not `1F80H`, (`MXCSR` with
+SSE only) in the compacted format of `RFBM` (`xCompact`), writes `XSTATE_BV` as `TO_BE_SAVED` and `XCOMP_BV` as
+`RFBM` with bit 63 set. Neither writes another header byte nor bytes 464–511; the bytes the formats leave reserved
+within a saved component are undefined. The stores are one masked store of the bytes written, after a check of the
+bytes `Profile.xTouched` gives (of the components saved, or of every component of `RFBM`): a fault leaves the area unwritten (the
+manuals do not say which bytes a faulting `XSAVE` writes). -/
