+/-! ## The instructions `XSAVE`, `XSAVEC` and `XRSTOR` (FV_7zip G1)
+
+What the instructions themselves do, after the SDM's Operation sections (Vol. 2, "XSAVE", "XSAVEC", "XRSTOR") and
+Vol. 1, ch. 13. The kernel's own saves and restores of a signal frame are above (`xsaveRuns`, `xrstor`); these
+functions take the register state as `X87` and `VecRegs`, which is what an instruction program reads. -/
+
+/-- The state components the model's `XSAVE`, `XSAVEC` and `XRSTOR` handle: those it holds (`xHeld`) but `PKRU`,
+which no instruction program reads or writes: x87, SSE, AVX, opmask, `ZMM_Hi256` and `Hi16_ZMM` (0, 1, 2, 5, 6,
+7). A requested-feature bitmap with another component is not modelled. -/
+def xInsnHeld : BitVec 64 := 0xE7
+
+/-- `Cpu.xInit` of the x87 state `x` and the vector state `v`, for the components in `xInsnHeld`. -/
+def xInitOf (x : X87) (v : VecRegs) (i : Nat) : Bool :=
+  let zs (lo hi : Nat) (f : BitVec 512 → Bool) := (List.range (hi - lo)).all fun n => f (v.zmm (Fin.ofNat 32 (lo + n)))
+  match i with
+  | 0 => x.fcw == 0x37F && x.fsw == 0 && x.full == 0 && (List.range 8).all fun j => x.st (Fin.ofNat 8 j) == 0
+  | 1 => zs 0 16 fun v => v.setWidth 128 == 0
+  | 2 => zs 0 16 fun v => v.extractLsb' 128 128 == 0
+  | 5 => (List.range 8).all fun j => v.k (Fin.ofNat 8 j) == 0
+  | 6 => zs 0 16 fun v => v.extractLsb' 256 256 == 0
+  | 7 => zs 16 32 fun v => v == 0
+  | _ => true
+
+/-- `XINUSE AND rfbm`, given `u` for the bits the manuals leave open: a component not in its initial configuration
+is in use (`xInitOf`); one in it may be either (SDM Vol. 1, 13.6). Unlike `Cpu.xInuseRequired`, `MXCSR` does not
+force SSE: "XINUSE[1] may be 0 even if MXCSR does not have its initial value of 1F80H" (SDM Vol. 2, "XSAVEC",
+footnote 1). -/
+def xInuseOf (x : X87) (v : VecRegs) (rfbm u : BitVec 64) : BitVec 64 :=
+  rfbm &&& (u ||| ofBitsLE 64 fun i => !xInitOf x v i)
+where
+  ofBitsLE (n : Nat) (f : Nat → Bool) : BitVec n :=
+    (List.range n).foldl (fun acc i => if f i then acc ||| ((1 : BitVec n) <<< i) else acc) 0
+
+/-- The extended components of the compacted format (SDM Vol. 1, 13.4.3) the model places: AVX, opmask, `ZMM_Hi256`,
+`Hi16_ZMM`. -/
+def xExtComps : List Nat := [2, 5, 6, 7]
+
+/-- The offset of component `i` in the compacted format of components `fmt`: from 576, each component `j` of `fmt`
+with `2 ≤ j < i` taking `CPUID.(EAX=0DH,ECX=j):EAX` bytes (SDM Vol. 2, "XSAVEC", "XRSTOR", Operation,
+`NEXT_FEATURE_OFFSET`). A component that `CPUID.(EAX=0DH,ECX=j):ECX[1]` says is 64-byte aligned in the compacted
+format (SDM Vol. 1, 13.4.3) is not modelled (`Profile.xCompAligned`). -/
+def Profile.xCompOffset (prof : Profile) (fmt : BitVec 64) (i : Nat) : Nat :=
+  ((List.range i).filter fun j => 2 ≤ j && fmt.getLsbD j).foldl (fun n j => n + prof.xSize j) 576
+
+/-- Whether a component of `fmt` is 64-byte aligned in the compacted format (`CPUID.(EAX=0DH,ECX=i):ECX[1]`, on
+CPU 0). -/
+def Profile.xCompAligned (prof : Profile) (fmt : BitVec 64) : Bool :=
+  (List.range 63).any fun j => 2 ≤ j && fmt.getLsbD j && (prof.cpuid 0 0xD (BitVec.ofNat 32 j)).ecx.getLsbD 1
+
+/-- The parts of the area (offset, length) an `XSAVE`, `XSAVEC` or `XRSTOR` accesses for the components `comps`: the
+legacy region and the header, and each extended component of `comps`, at its offset in the standard format or
+(`compact`) in the compacted format of `fmt`. The manuals say only which components are saved or loaded; whether a
+processor also checks the bytes of those requested but not saved or loaded (`comps` the requested-feature bitmap,
+for a compacted `XRSTOR` within the format `fmt`) is a choice of the instructions' programs, as measured (FV_7zip G1,
+`tools/xsavetest`): an Intel Core i7-14650HX raises `#PF` for an `XRSTOR` whose `XSTATE_BV` initializes AVX, or an
+`XSAVEC` with AVX in its initial configuration, whose AVX bytes run into an unmapped page; an AMD EPYC 9V45 does not
+for a compacted `XRSTOR`'s initialized components. -/
+def Profile.xTouched (prof : Profile) (compact : Bool) (fmt comps : BitVec 64) : List (Nat × Nat) :=
+  (0, 576) :: (xExtComps.filter (comps.getLsbD ·)).map fun i =>
+    (if compact then prof.xCompOffset fmt i else prof.xOffset i, prof.xSize i)
