+/-- What an `XRSTOR` does with the area whose header has `XSTATE_BV` `bv` and `XCOMP_BV` `comp`, for the
+requested-feature bitmap `rfbm` (SDM Vol. 2, "XRSTOR", Operation): the form (compacted if `XCOMP_BV[63]`), the
+compacted format's components (`fmt`), the components it loads (`restore`) and those it initializes (`init`), and
+whether it loads `MXCSR` (the standard form whenever `rfbm` has SSE or AVX; the compacted form with SSE's load). -/
+structure XPlan where
+  compact : Bool
+  fmt : BitVec 64
+  restore : BitVec 64
+  init : BitVec 64
+  loadsMx : Bool
